1j53|n|Honor; grace; favor; mercy; clemency; happy augry. ; The native form of a metal, whether free and uncombined, as gold, copper, etc., or combined, as iron, lead, etc. Usually the ores contain the metals combined with oxygen, sulphur, arsenic, etc. (called mineralizers). ; A native metal or its compound with the rock in which it occurs, after it has been picked over to throw out what is worthless. ; Metal; as, the liquid ore.	a:1f74,16,1~1f74,16,1
